# Git flow

- `develop` is always ahead of (or equal to) `main`. Daily work lands on `develop` first.
- `main` is the last released/stable line. Do not commit features to `main`. Promote with `git checkout main` then `git merge --no-ff develop` only when you intend a release.
- One branch per product-scope item: `feature/<short-slug>` (example: `feature/connect-ldap`).
- Branch from current `develop`. Do not stack unrelated work on one branch.
- Commit on the feature branch (why, not what). No `--no-verify`, no `git config` changes, no force-push to `main` or `develop`.
- When the item is done: `git checkout develop` then `git merge --no-ff feature/<slug>`.
- Do not open a PR or push unless asked.
- Never mix LDAP writes, Entra, or a fifth workspace onto a UI-polish branch.
